WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.520
Scrambled egg whites,
a vegetable smoothie

00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:05.120
or wholegrain cereal
with low fat milk.

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:07.120
That’s how pop megastar Beyoncé

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:09.960
described a bootylicious breakfast
a few years ago.

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:15.200
However eating cereal has declined
by over 11% over the past five years,

00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:18.560
with 40% of millennials
dismissing it as inconvenient

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:20.280
because it involves washing up.

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:24.240
Meanwhile the kind of farming
that produces bacon and sausages

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:26.800
is criticised for contributing
to climate change

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:28.960
through the carbon
emissions it produces.

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:31.080
So by the year 2039

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:34.240
meat, cereal and even dairy
may be much harder to find

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:35.400
on the breakfast menu.

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:38.520
Instead, you might be
tucking into a plate of...

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:43.000
According to researchers
in the Netherlands,

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:45.240
insects cost less
to raise than cattle,

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:48.840
consume less water and don’t
really leave a carbon footprint.

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:51.280
Plus in many cultures
around the world,

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:54.240
in fact 30% of the
planet’s population,

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:56.560
they’re already considered
pretty tasty.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:59.800
Robyn Shapiro,
founder of Seek Food says...

00:01:04.840 --> 00:01:08.240
So, while a rasher of bacon
may become an illicit luxury

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:10.520
only available in a fancy restaurant,

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:12.480
crunchy nut cricket flakes

00:01:12.560 --> 00:01:15.080
could mean starting the day
with a bowl of creepy crawlies

00:01:15.160 --> 00:01:16.720
from your garden biosphere.

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:19.640
Probably not if you’re vegan
or vegetarian

00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:21.440
like one in eight Britons now are.

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:25.480
Or how about lab meat
grown from animal stem cells,

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:29.120
with no need for real-life pigs or
chickens to become dead ones.

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:32.840
A guilt free slice of black pudding
where there’s blood on the plate

00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:34.600
but not on your hands.

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:37.040
Maybe the thought of this
has you desperately reaching

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:39.600
for that one cup of coffee
you’re allowed per year

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:41.720
thanks to climate change rationing.

00:01:41.800 --> 00:01:44.840
Researchers and chefs
including Heston Blumenthal,

00:01:44.920 --> 00:01:48.200
have discovered that what
you hear can affect what you taste.

00:01:48.520 --> 00:01:52.160
So in 2039, your coffee might
seem like its full of sugar

00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:54.120
even though there
isn’t anything sweet in it

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:57.040
apart from the sound of music.

00:01:57.720 --> 00:02:00.400
With immersive dining
experiences on the rise,

00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:03.680
from medieval banquets
to murder mystery stories,

00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:07.000
or even a gastro physics
journey through space,

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:10.320
could breakfast of the future
be less about traditional taste

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:12.400
and more about living out
your culinary dreams

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:14.560
in a flavour-filled fantasy land?

00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:20.960
By 2039 it looks like most of us,
70% in fact, will live in cities.

00:02:21.320 --> 00:02:24.240
To cut transport costs, maybe
we’ll want to grow the onions

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:26.800
to go with our stem cell
sausages more locally.

00:02:27.320 --> 00:02:30.240
However, if the current
housing crisis continues

00:02:30.320 --> 00:02:33.040
and luxury flats fill in
every remaining space,

00:02:33.560 --> 00:02:35.560
where would we plant our greens?

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:38.920
Perhaps the answer is underground.

00:02:39.560 --> 00:02:42.600
In cities around the world,
this is already happening.

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:45.640
Urban farmers swap
sunlight for LED light

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:49.600
and use a system called hydroponics
where plants are grown in water,

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:52.880
so there’s no need for soil,
despite being surrounded by it.

00:02:53.160 --> 00:02:54.720
Perfect for farming seaweed,

00:02:55.120 --> 00:02:58.640
widely considered a sustainable
superfood of the future.

00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:03.080
With cities increasingly full of
people and traffic by 2039,

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:05.880
we may need new ways
to transport the ingredients

00:03:05.960 --> 00:03:07.600
that end up in our breakfasts.

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:09.840
Could this be where drones fly in?

00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:12.680
Following the rise of
takeaway delivery services,

00:03:12.760 --> 00:03:15.120
a company in China
has been trialling drones

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:17.160
as a way of getting
food to customers.

00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:21.920
If this takes off, maybe delivery
drivers will be a thing of the past.

00:03:22.280 --> 00:03:26.320
However, would you be happy to have
a drone rather than a person

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:30.440
popping by with your music-infused
coffee or seaweed sandwich spread?

00:03:30.840 --> 00:03:33.520
With increasing numbers
of us working flexibly,

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:36.520
perhaps the need for a quick
breakfast before dashing off to work

00:03:36.600 --> 00:03:38.160
will no longer be necessary.

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:41.680
Maybe instead we’ll start
to actually treat breakfast

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:44.040
as the most important meal of the day

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:45.920
rather than just talking about it.

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:48.360
But whatever’s on your
wheat bran plate,

00:03:48.440 --> 00:03:50.800
you probably won’t have
to wash it up afterwards

00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:52.600
because you’ll be able to eat it.

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:55.640
Great news for if you’re
a 57-year-old millennial.

00:03:58.360 --> 00:04:03.740
Thanks for watching. 
Don’t forget to subscribe! :)

